## What makes a test positive or negative?
A test is positive when the test value used is the expected value the program requires from the users
A test is negative when the test value used is an unexpected value the program does not expect from the user

## Why can a negative test pass?
This is to ensure that even in a negative test, the program catches the unexpected result to prevent unexpected outcomes, errors or crashes

